{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/865036-luddites","id":865036,"title":"Luddites","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-13T11:38:41-07:00","id":865036,"title":"Luddites","content":"In the early 1800s a group of former mill workers found themselves disenfranchised by the ever quickening pace of industry and progress. Deprived of their livehood by machine that performed their jobs more quickly, the group came to protest the increasing industrialization of their homeland in the name of all those left behind. Naming themselves after the semi-mythical Ned Ludd, a figure supposedly haunting the Sherwood Forest like a latter day Robin Hood, the Luddites took to raiding nearby factories and smashing the hateful machines that had replaced them. The roots of the compact that bears this name has its origins in one such raid in the spring of 1812, where events took a turn irrevocably into the macabre.<br /> <br /> Within the confines of a seemingly normal factory the Luddites found a machine. Not the expected rows of industrial spinning frames congruent with their era. No, what lay before them was a nightmare of churning gears, moving platforms, churning pistons, and sparking circuits rising up in a mechnical sea miles high (far beyond what the little factory they had entered should have been capable of containing). The room was black as pitch, yet a pale blue glow like moonlight suffused the entire infernal mechanism. <br /> <br /> Not even the most learned scholar truly understands what the God-Machine is. None of the men gaping at the device could have put what they were seeing into words. But humanity has a fallback option in such circumstances. Most who see the gears turning choose to flee and attempt to forget. Some fall to their knees and beg for mercy. But not these men. It seems on some level they recognized the nature of the machine without comprehending it. They saw in the turning gyres and sinister hisses of the thing a familiar uncaring, unrelenting push they knew very well. Progress had abused them terribly, took them in and wore them down and discarded them like so much garbage when it had no further need of them. They had been victims of the cold merciless whims of industrial forces, pawns in a game none of them understood. And they had all railed against those forces. They had never seen the God-Machine, but they had felt the weight of its manipulations crushing down on them all their lives. Perhaps that is why instinct led them to grip their hammers all the more tightly and as one step forward. <br /> <br /> The death toll was heavy that night. There were things in the darkness that screamed like steam escaping from a pipe, things that ripped and tore and broke bones. But the company was large and skilled at striking hard and fast at their targets. Come the morning the secret machine had come crashing down, the mill which housed it seemingly burned in a fire. Of the few who made it out alive the world had changed. Their cause was no longer about ruined lives and lost wages. Their enemy was more terrible and heartless than they had imagined, looking to humanity not even as slave labor but as raw materials to be burned up. The stakes were now reality itself. The war upon the machine had begun.<br /> <br /> Just something I imagined up while waiting for The Year Without a Summer. Focus of the society will be Demons and Prometheans alongside other entities with ties to the Principal and the God-Machine. May incorporate Lord Byron and Ada Lovelace into this insanity depending on how Dark Eras treats them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T00:36:28-07:00","id":865359,"title":"","content":"sounds like a good concept. Waiting to see how it would turn out","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T02:54:53-07:00","id":865384,"title":"","content":"It's pretty inaccurate to history, but it's a pretty neat idea none the less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T21:54:43-